  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Seminar on Mastering Negotiation Skills for Counterterrorism and Regional Security Cooperation 01-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The workshop for security practitioners will focus on understanding how to negotiate effectively, to gain a competitive advantage, achieve national objectives, and effect change. In Mastering Negotiation Skills, participants will learn negotiation strategies to understand, plan, and achieve objectives in a variety of contexts including conflict scenarios and reconciliation initiatives. Participants will engage in real-time negotiations and receive feedback in real time. Beyond learning the frameworks and skills associated with negotiating, participants will practice putting these new skills into action. Elements of the course will use the bestselling work of Roger Fisher titled, Getting to Yes: Negotiating Agreement Without Giving.</narrative>
  </description>
